course: dictionary
lesson: 9479
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word stave is a good example. It can mean lines for music, a strip of wood, a stick, or a verb with a phrase attached.
explain: «Written music is a map of sound: notes sit on five lines called a staff (or stave), and the higher a note sits, the higher it sounds.» Here the words written, notes and sound tell you that a stave is the set of five lines for music, not a stick.
explain: Now look at «We ate apples to stave off hunger.» Stave off is a phrase. The words hunger and ate tell you it means to stop something happening for a while. Try your meaning in the sentence: "We ate apples to stop hunger for a while." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A stave is the set of five lines on which music notes are written (in the US this is called a staff).
fact: A stave is also one of the curved wooden strips that make the sides of a barrel or wooden bucket.
fact: A stave can be a strong stick or pole.
fact: «Stave off» means to stop something happening for a while, as in «We ate apples to stave off hunger.»
fact: «Stave in» means to break a hole in something by hitting it. The plural of stave is staves.
exercise: «Written music is a map of sound: notes sit on five lines called a staff (or stave).» In this sentence, what is a stave? | *The five lines that music notes are written on | A strong stick for walking | A way to stop hunger | A wooden barrel
exercise: «We ate apples to stave off hunger.» What does stave off mean? | *To stop hunger for a while | To climb a ladder | To write a tune | To make a hole in a bucket
exercise: Which word is the plural of stave? | stavings | staffs | staved | *staves
test: «The cooper bent each curved wooden stave into place before he closed the barrel.» What is a stave here? | *One curved wooden strip of the barrel | A hole in the side | A line on which music is written | A pole used to climb
test: «The angry crowd tried to stave in the old wooden door.» What does stave in mean? | To stop the door for a while | To paint the door | To hang music notes on it | *To break a hole in it by hitting it
exam: «The music teacher pointed to the stave and said, "Sing the notes from the bottom line up."» What does stave mean here? | A curved strip of a barrel | A strong stick or pole | *The set of five lines for writing music | To stop something for a while
